# netsurf: the structural check by direction and position (patch 380)
# Generated 2026-11-06
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 379)
#
# The r104 census: 379's scoped check found real matches -- youtube 6,
# guardian 1. A temporary trace: youtube's is a bare :first-child rule
# matching <body>'s first child (div.bdcvod) while <iframe>s are appended
# at the end of <body>; guardian's a div:first-child on <body>'s first div
# while a <script> is appended. A child inserted or removed at the end
# cannot change which child is first.
#
#  - Each structural compound knows what its pseudo-class depends on:
#    being the first (:first-child, :first-of-type), being the last
#    (:last-child, :last-of-type), the count of earlier siblings
#    (:nth-child, :nth-of-type), of later ones (:nth-last-*), or both
#    (:only-*).
#  - html_rl_block_struct_risk, given where the change sits among the
#    parent's element children (the inserted elements, or a removed
#    block's element neighbour -- the end if none), tests only the
#    children such a rule can flip: the child that is or was the first
#    (of its type) when the change reaches the start; the last when it
#    reaches the end; those after the change for an earlier-count rule;
#    those before it for a later-count one. The moved elements themselves
#    are built afresh.
#  - Positions are used only for a child-list mark on this very parent.
#    A removal's place: removeChild (macsurf_qjs.c) now records the
#    removed child's next element sibling (NULL: it was the last) and
#    marks through macos9_js_mark_dom_dirty_removal; the mark slot holds it
#    as a node reference (rm_next / rm_state, primary and extra marks,
#    released with the slot's other references), and a second removal
#    from the same parent in the batch makes it unknown. youtube removes a
#    box-less <script> from <body> in the same batch as it appends an
#    <iframe>: without the place, that removal took the whole range and
#    declined the batch. Unknown places (other removal paths, two
#    removals), a removed block beside an inline container, and any other
#    mark take the whole range, as 379.
#  - The first / last rules are exact: the first child flips if it is
#    first now and something removed preceded it, or it was first and new
#    elements precede it now; the last, the mirror. *-of-type ones keep
#    the range test.
#  - A structural pseudo-class inside :not() / :is() / :where() /
#    :matches() is bounded by the OUTER compound (its tag, id, classes),
#    which keeps the element; 379 made every such one unbounded. The
#    compound scan backwards now steps over balanced (...) groups:
#    .x:not(.y):not(:last-of-type) is one compound, not
#    :not(:last-of-type). youtube's remaining decline was such a rule.
#
# Result on a 2500-paragraph sim page with a bare :first-child rule: an
# <iframe> appended to <body> 170 -> 32 ms; a <script> 167 -> 4 ms. On
# youtube the structural declines fall 5 -> 1.
#
